{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf","id":609583,"title":"Crossover Query: Vampire Kiss on a Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-31T09:23:27-07:00","id":609583,"title":"Crossover Query: Vampire Kiss on a Werewolf","content":"What would be the effect of a vampire kiss on a Werewolf? It's very effective on mortals, and even on other vampires (need to roll instinct/self-control difficulty 8). Any idea how this would work on werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:58:16-07:00","id":609654,"title":"","content":"From Memory, the rules from Werewolf: The Dark Ages said roll Willpower or Rage, Dif 8 to resist. I don't know if there's been an update since then. Also, keep in mind Vampires need to grapple first before being allowed to bite.<br /> I cant seem to find anything to contradict W:tDA in DA:Werewolf or W20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:45:52-07:00","id":609844,"title":"","content":"Can't find anything to contradict the Dark Ages reference, except that it is also mentioned that vampires generally aren't going to get the chance to pull that particular stunt if the werewolf's pack is anywhere nearby -- in the sense that the Kiss is difficult to accomplish with a pack of pissed-off werewolves trying to tear you limb from limb.<br /> <br /> On a slight aside: remember that ghouling a werewolf is next to impossible as they're (generally) violently allergic to Vitae, and will begin projectile-vomiting any that they ingest -- and although not specified, the way it's written tends to imply a Frenzy is a possible outcome. The optional rule for determining if the werewolf in question is one of the few that <i>can</i> ingest Vitae is as follows: Roll Gnosis vs. difficulty 3. A failure or botch indicates that the werewolf may consume Vitae without ill-effect (and it is hinted in various places that he may use Vitae to gain advantages from it as any other Ghoul would).<br /> <br /> Actually Embracing a werewolf is rather more difficult (and potentially dangerous for the vampire). The werewolf (or really anyone with Gnosis) may roll Gnosis to resist at difficulty 6. A success indicates the werewolf dies peacefully and without pain. A failure indicates he dies violently and in agony. A botch results in a vampiric werewolf (an &quot;Abomination&quot;). A Willpower point may be spent for an automatic success.<br /> <br /> Other werewolf/vampire trivia: A werewolf has 20 points of blood to feed from rather than the 10 for an ordinary human, and this goes to 25 in Crinos (and possibly Hispo) form. A vampire consuming werewolf blood has an increased chance of frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 07-31-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:43:08-07:00","id":609978,"title":"","content":"To be precise, +1 difficulty to rolls to resist Frenzy from the vampire part for each BP of werewolf blood in her system.<br /> <br /> And spending this blood gives you some extra bonus for the turn, based on the werewolf Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> I remember a character of mine that lived almost exclusively from werewolf blood. Each willpower point I could get where destined to resist frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:07:37-07:00","id":610062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=609978#post609978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be precise, +1 difficulty to rolls to resist Frenzy from the vampire part for each BP of werewolf blood in her system.<br /> <br /> And spending this blood gives you some extra bonus for the turn, based on the werewolf Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> I remember a character of mine that lived almost exclusively from werewolf blood. Each willpower point I could get where destined to resist frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point #2 highlights a really dumb crossover mechanic that has no basis in Werewolf (Pure Breed has no correlation to power). Point #3 is hard to believe, seeing as how Garou aren't exactly common. Or safe to feed from.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:14:27-07:00","id":610071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610062#post610062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Point #3 is hard to believe, seeing as how Garou aren't exactly common. Or safe to feed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily (although certainly in a general sense). There was an example in Outcasts where a Ronin Garou and a Caitiff Kindred who (at least for a time) traveled together and the former willingly fed the latter so that he would not have to feed from innocent humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:19:59-07:00","id":610226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=609844#post609844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a slight aside: remember that ghouling a werewolf is next to impossible as they're (generally) violently allergic to Vitae, and will begin projectile-vomiting any that they ingest -- and although not specified, the way it's written tends to imply a Frenzy is a possible outcome. The optional rule for determining if the werewolf in question is one of the few that <i>can</i> ingest Vitae is as follows: Roll Gnosis vs. difficulty 3. A failure or botch indicates that the werewolf may consume Vitae without ill-effect (and it is hinted in various places that he may use Vitae to gain advantages from it as any other Ghoul would).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious where this option system came from. I know it is sometimes stated that Garou are allergic. I didn't know of such a specific system. And if you can get a Garou to keep down the blood, they absolutely can be ghouled. That actually isn't in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=609844#post609844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually Embracing a werewolf is rather more difficult (and potentially dangerous for the vampire). The werewolf (or really anyone with Gnosis) may roll Gnosis to resist at difficulty 6. A success indicates the werewolf dies peacefully and without pain. A failure indicates he dies violently and in agony. A botch results in a vampiric werewolf (an &quot;Abomination&quot;). A Willpower point may be spent for an automatic success.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm fairly positive that you cannot spend Willpower on this roll. I seem to remember it being stated that nothing short of a Celestine could attempt to influence the roll to become an Abomination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=609844#post609844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Other werewolf/vampire trivia: A werewolf has 20 points of blood to feed from rather than the 10 for an ordinary human, and this goes to 25 in Crinos (and possibly Hispo) form. A vampire consuming werewolf blood has an increased chance of frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div> This system always struck me as a bit odd. And brings up the question of drinking blood amounts and gaining blood points. The blood point system is supposed to be an abstraction. But it is stated that 1 blood point is approximately 1 pint of blood for humans. So does a Garou have 20 pints? does each pint given grant 2 Vitae? Is it possible the Vampire drinks 3 blood points, but gains the nourishment of 6? The simplest system is to just say its 1 for 1, but it does raise some questions if you think too much about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=609978#post609978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be precise, +1 difficulty to rolls to resist Frenzy from the vampire part for each BP of werewolf blood in her system.<br /> <br /> And spending this blood gives you some extra bonus for the turn, based on the werewolf Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> I remember a character of mine that lived almost exclusively from werewolf blood. Each willpower point I could get where destined to resist frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To to address these....The first part is correct. The penalty also applies to R\u00f6tschreck<i>.</i><br /> The second is not really true. There are rumors that Pure Lupine blood can grant bonuses. I haven't ever seen a system for it. And in theory, the bonuses would last for as long as the blood is in your system, not for a turn (same as the Frenzy mechanic).<br /> I flat out find the third state hard to believe. You would have had to have an extremely forgiving ST. And no amount of Willpower expenditure will stave off Frenzy/R\u00f6tschreck for any real length of time when all of the rolls are at +10 dif (full of Lupine blood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:27:53-07:00","id":610314,"title":"","content":"The Pure Breed blood bonus is strictly something that VTM projects onto crossover. It's in the Vampire ST Handbook, but not the one for Werewolf, because, as stated, it's incredibly damned bizarre and has no grounding, rhyme or reason. As for the extra blood, that apparently comes from mystical power, and actually seems to insulate the Garou and Fera from having too much blood taken; most systems seem to have the Changers taking half the damage that a human would, such as in reference to the Thaumaturgy powers such as Theft of Vitae or Cauldron of Blood.<br /> <br /> The vitae allergy can be found on page 197 of the Revised Werewolf ST Handbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:56:00-07:00","id":610435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610226#post610226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This system always struck me as a bit odd. And brings up the question of drinking blood amounts and gaining blood points. The blood point system is supposed to be an abstraction. But it is stated that 1 blood point is approximately 1 pint of blood for humans. So does a Garou have 20 pints? does each pint given grant 2 Vitae? Is it possible the Vampire drinks 3 blood points, but gains the nourishment of 6? The simplest system is to just say its 1 for 1, but it does raise some questions if you think too much about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elder vampires have more blood points without having more blood, because their vitae is more concentrated/potent/higher quality, etc... Werewolves would be the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:46:58-07:00","id":610504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610226#post610226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious where this option system came from. I know it is sometimes stated that Garou are allergic. I didn't know of such a specific system.</div> </div> </div> </div>SOS already said it, but yeah, page 197 Storyteller's Handbook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610226#post610226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you can get a Garou to keep down the blood, they absolutely can be ghouled. That actually isn't in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, y'know...<i> if</i>. Now granted, the Gnosis roll as to whether or not the Garou in question can ingest Vitae<i> is </i>an optional rule, but it's mentioned all over that werewolves and vampire-blood don't mix generally. So, I feel that excepting some storyteller ruling, it absolutely <i>is</i> in question.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610226#post610226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly positive that you cannot spend Willpower on this roll. I seem to remember it being stated that nothing short of a Celestine could attempt to influence the roll to become an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gaia grants Her favored children one final chance to escape the living death. A Garou can make a Gnosis roll, difficulty 6, to die quietly. If the roll succeeds, he dies without pain and his spirit travels to its destined place. If the roll fails, he dies in tortuous agony, but his spirit is free. If the roll botches, the Garou becomes an Abomination and cannot hope to ever see his Tribal Homeland. No Discipline, Gift, magick, or any other sort of power short of direct intervention by a Celestine can affect this roll, save one -- <b>the werewolf can spend a willpower point to gain an automatic success as usual (and is almost certain to do so)</b>.&quot; Players' Handbook, page 191. A virtually identical passage may be found in the Storyteller's Handbook, page 198.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T01:41:33-07:00","id":610559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610504#post610504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Gaia grants Her favored children one final chance to escape the living death. A Garou can make a Gnosis roll, difficulty 6, to die quietly. If the roll succeeds, he dies without pain and his spirit travels to its destined place. If the roll fails, he dies in tortuous agony, but his spirit is free. If the roll botches, the Garou becomes an Abomination and cannot hope to ever see his Tribal Homeland. No Discipline, Gift, magick, or any other sort of power short of direct intervention by a Celestine can affect this roll, save one -- <b>the werewolf can spend a willpower point to gain an automatic success as usual (and is almost certain to do so)</b>.&quot; Players' Handbook, page 191. A virtually identical passage may be found in the Storyteller's Handbook, page 198.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thanks. Having not read most of the books in depth in over a decade leads to misremembering stuff sometimes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So yea, spend Willpower then to avoid Abomination as well as nothing short of a Celestine being able to interfere. Seems kind of contrary to me, but just makes it that much smaller of a chance of happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:21:23-07:00","id":610590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point #2 highlights a really dumb crossover mechanic that has no basis in Werewolf (Pure Breed has no correlation to power). Point #3 is hard to believe, seeing as how Garou aren't exactly common. Or safe to feed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed about point #2. I don't use it myself and can't remember from what book precisely, just that was one of those with crossover mechanics from Revised era, or maybe it was just a house-rule and my memory is tricking me, it happens. Also agreed about point #3, but it happened in the game. You can complain with my ST if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily (although certainly in a general sense). There was an example in Outcasts where a Ronin Garou and a Caitiff Kindred who (at least for a time) traveled together and the former willingly fed the latter so that he would not have to feed from innocent humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case, I was a prisioner, and eventualy ally, in a Garou Caern. At the time I arrived almost everyone in the Caern, elders included, where PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious where this option system came from. I know it is sometimes stated that Garou are allergic. I didn't know of such a specific system. And if you can get a Garou to keep down the blood, they absolutely can be ghouled. That actually isn't in question.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly positive that you cannot spend Willpower on this roll. I seem to remember it being stated that nothing short of a Celestine could attempt to influence the roll to become an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I remember the same rules he posted. A change between editions, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This system always struck me as a bit odd. And brings up the question of drinking blood amounts and gaining blood points. The blood point system is supposed to be an abstraction. But it is stated that 1 blood point is approximately 1 pint of blood for humans. So does a Garou have 20 pints? does each pint given grant 2 Vitae? Is it possible the Vampire drinks 3 blood points, but gains the nourishment of 6? The simplest system is to just say its 1 for 1, but it does raise some questions if you think too much about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By myself, I found easier to consider that the system is always talking about the Vitae, the mystical energy truly consumed, and the amount of blood is completely vague. Even for humans it is just a common estimation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I flat out find the third state hard to believe. You would have had to have an extremely forgiving ST. And no amount of Willpower expenditure will stave off Frenzy/R\u00f6tschreck for any real length of time when all of the rolls are at +10 dif (full of Lupine blood).</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST a little forgiving + PC werewolves seeing no problem in keeping a vampire around + the ST didn't called that much Frenzy rolls to begin with. And my dif was at +15, 8th gen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure Breed blood bonus is strictly something that VTM projects onto crossover. It's in the Vampire ST Handbook, but not the one for Werewolf, because, as stated, it's incredibly damned bizarre and has no grounding, rhyme or reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now I remember from where it comes. There are already crossover rules to override this one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:07:31-07:00","id":610994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610590#post610590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST a little forgiving + PC werewolves seeing no problem in keeping a vampire around</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes <i>me</i> want to frenzy at +15 difficulty<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:35:24-07:00","id":611350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610314#post610314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most systems seem to have the Changers taking half the damage that a human would, such as in reference to the Thaumaturgy powers such as Theft of Vitae or Cauldron of Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that regarding Theft of Vitae since the blood it's drawing out is more potent than that of normal humans, and so less would be needed, as with stealing blood from elder vampires. But I'd imagine that Cauldron of Blood deals the same actual damage that it normally would, the werewolf just has more blood points to spare so losing 5+ wouldn't automatically put them in the ICU. (Being able to soak the aggravated damage from having one's blood boiled at all is already a big advantage over a human target.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:07:39-07:00","id":611432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=611350#post611350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that regarding Theft of Vitae since the blood it's drawing out is more potent than that of normal humans, and so less would be needed, as with stealing blood from elder vampires. But I'd imagine that Cauldron of Blood deals the same actual damage that it normally would, the werewolf just has more blood points to spare so losing 5+ wouldn't automatically put them in the ICU. (Being able to soak the aggravated damage from having one's blood boiled at all is already a big advantage over a human target.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but the text of the effect for the ST Handbook says one level per two blood points for CoB, so it seems to work out to &quot;requires more work to try to injure them&quot;. It's good to be half-spirit, or in other words, half of something that Kindred can't really get too great a grip on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T23:35:19-07:00","id":611931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=610994#post610994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes <i>me</i> want to frenzy at +15 difficulty</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Are you a Garou yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:11:18-07:00","id":612233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/609583-crossover-query-vampire-kiss-on-a-werewolf?p=611931#post611931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Are you a Garou yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously not, or else it would be at <i>-15</i> difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}